---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Church | True Orthodox, Old Calendar, RGV TX"
  description="St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Church — a True Orthodox parish in Bayview, TX serving the Rio Grande Valley. Old Calendar, Apostolic tradition, faithful to the Catacomb Church and the New Martyrs."
>
  <!-- ==================== INTRO ==================== -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 md:py-28">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-tan-dark">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl text-text-primary md:text-4xl">
      About St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Church
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 font-display italic text-lg text-text-primary/80 md:text-xl">
      True Orthodox &middot; Old Calendar &middot; Faithful to the Apostolic Tradition
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
      <p>
        St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Church in the Rio Grande Valley is a
        mission of the True Orthodox Church, preserving the unbroken faith,
        worship, and discipline of the Orthodox Church as handed down from
        the Holy Apostles, safeguarded by the Seven Ecumenical Councils, and
        defended by the New Martyrs and Confessors of the 20th century.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our parish stands within the Apostolic and Catacomb tradition of those
        who resisted the modern departures of Ecumenism, Modernism, and
        Sergianism &mdash; the same three errors consistently condemned in the
        authoritative history of our Metropolia.
      </p>
      <p>
        We trace our ecclesial lineage through the Old Calendarist Greek
        Church, aided by hierarchs of the Russian Church Abroad, and
        confirmed in autonomy for missionary work in the West. For this
        reason, we hold fast to the Julian (Old) Calendar, the ancient
        liturgical life of the Church, and the fullness of Holy Tradition
        without alteration or compromise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto h-px w-full max-w-3xl border-0 bg-liturgical-current opacity-40" />

  <!-- ==================== WORSHIP & PARISH LIFE ==================== -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-text-primary md:text-4xl">
      Our Worship and Parish Life
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
      <p>
        We gather each week to celebrate the Divine Liturgy, to keep the
        feasts of the Church, and to live the Orthodox Christian life as it
        has been lived for centuries.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our parish worships exclusively according to the traditional Eastern
        Orthodox rite, preserving the prayers, hymns, and sacred actions
        that have formed the heart of Orthodox life since the earliest
        centuries.
      </p>
      <p>Here, the faithful find:</p>
      <ul class="ml-6 space-y-2 text-text-primary/85">
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          the Holy Mysteries offered in their ancient form
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          the ascetical and sacramental life of Orthodoxy
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          the unchanged teachings of the Holy Fathers
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          a refuge from the spiritual confusion of the modern world
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        St. John of Kronstadt Church exists to bring the Apostolic Faith to
        all people &mdash; whether returning to the faith of their ancestors
        or discovering Orthodoxy for the first time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto h-px w-full max-w-3xl border-0 bg-liturgical-current opacity-40" />

  <!-- ==================== OUR PASTOR ==================== -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-text-primary md:text-4xl">Our Pastor</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
      <p>
        Our pastor, Priest Antonios Altermatt, has served the community for a
        decade with dedication and pastoral care. Through his leadership,
        Archpriest Antonios fosters a parish life marked by reverence,
        fellowship, and spiritual growth, guiding all who come to St. John&apos;s
        toward a deeper encounter with Christ and His Holy Church.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto h-px w-full max-w-3xl border-0 bg-liturgical-current opacity-40" />

  <!-- ==================== IDENTITY AS TRUE ORTHODOX ==================== -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-text-primary md:text-4xl">
      Our Identity as True Orthodox
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
      <p>
        St. John of Kronstadt Church stands firmly within the confession of
        the True Orthodox Church, upholding:
      </p>
      <ul class="ml-6 space-y-2 text-text-primary/85">
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          the Old Calendar
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          the fullness of Apostolic and Patristic Tradition
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          the rejection of Ecumenism, Modernism, and Sergianism
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          the continuity of the Catacomb Church
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          the missionary calling to restore Orthodoxy in the West
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We are a parish for all who seek the fullness of the Orthodox Christian
        Faith, without innovation, without compromise, and without submission
        to the errors that have overtaken much of the modern religious world.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto h-px w-full max-w-3xl border-0 bg-liturgical-current opacity-40" />

  <!-- ==================== OUR MISSION ==================== -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-text-primary md:text-4xl">Our Mission</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
      <p>We exist to:</p>
      <ul class="ml-6 space-y-2 text-text-primary/85">
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          proclaim the Gospel of Christ
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          preserve the ancient Orthodox faith
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          offer the Holy Mysteries in purity
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          form a community of repentance, prayer, and love
        </li>
        <li class="relative pl-6">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 top-0 text-sacred-gold">☩</span>
          bring the Apostolic Church to the people of the Rio Grande Valley
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Church is a beacon of traditional
        Orthodoxy, rooted in the witness of the Catacomb Saints and the True
        Orthodox Church, standing firm in the faith once delivered to the
        saints.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto h-px w-full max-w-3xl border-0 bg-liturgical-current opacity-40" />

  <!-- ==================== SERVICES & SCHEDULE ==================== -->
  <section id="schedule" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl scroll-mt-20 px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-tan-dark">Visit</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl text-text-primary md:text-4xl">Services &amp; Schedule</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>
    <dl class="mt-6 divide-y divide-border-soft border-y border-border-soft">
      <div class="py-4">
        <dt class="font-display text-lg text-text-primary">Vespers</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-text-primary/85">Saturday evenings &middot; 5:00 PM</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="py-4">
        <dt class="font-display text-lg text-text-primary">Divine Liturgy</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-text-primary/85">Sunday mornings &middot; 9:00 AM</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="mt-6 text-text-primary/75">
      Questions about visiting? Call
      <a href="tel:+19564490225">(956) 449-0225</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto h-px w-full max-w-3xl border-0 bg-liturgical-current opacity-40" />

  <!-- ==================== CANONICAL STANDING ==================== -->
  <section id="communion" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl scroll-mt-20 px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-tan-dark">Our Canonical Family</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl text-text-primary md:text-4xl">Canonical Standing</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
      St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Mission is a parish of the Autonomous
      Orthodox Metropolia of North and South America and the British Isles
      (True Orthodox). We are in canonical communion with the Avlona Synod
      USA and the IPC Katakomb Church.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
